/* ==============================================================================
   CyberRisk Intelligence — Global Cybersecurity Threats (2015–2024)
   DAX Measures & Implementation Notes
   Author: Alwin Meniens
   ============================================================================== */

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measure 1: Total Financial Impact
// Visual usage: KPI Card, Line Chart Y-axis, Country Bar Chart X/Y, Industry Bar Chart
// Column in dataset: 'Financial Loss (in Million $)'
// Note: Each record represents an incident whose financial loss is in millions of USD ($M).
// The sum across all 3,000 recorded incidents is ~151,478.91 (i.e. ~$151.48 Billion).
// In Power BI, this is displayed with 'K' units on the KPI card ($151.48K M = $151.48B).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Total Financial Impact = 
SUM('Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024'[Financial Loss (in Million $)])


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measure 2: Total Cybersecurity Incidents
// Visual usage: KPI Card (Top-Left)
// Represents the total count of reported threat events in the filtered context.
// Total dataset records: 3,000 incidents (displayed as '3K' on the KPI card).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Total Cybersecurity Incidents = 
COUNTROWS('Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024')


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measure 3: Average Response Time
// Visual usage: KPI Card (Top-Right)
// Column in dataset: 'Incident Resolution Time (in Hours)'
// Model/Formula mapping note:
// In the Kaggle dataset, the underlying column is named 'Incident Resolution Time (in Hours)'.
// If renamed during Power Query ETL to 'Response Time (Hours)', use that column name.
// Both variations are documented below for complete implementation transparency.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Variant A (Direct Dataset Column):
Average Response Time = 
AVERAGE('Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024'[Incident Resolution Time (in Hours)])

// Variant B (If column was renamed to 'Response Time (Hours)' in Power Query):
// Average Response Time = 
// AVERAGE('Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024'[Response Time (Hours)])


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measure 4: Total Data Breached (Model vs. Underlying Dataset Column Mapping)
// Visual usage: KPI Card (Second from Left, displaying '2bn')
// Verification finding:
// In the Kaggle dataset 'Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024.csv', the column tracking
// breach magnitude is 'Number of Affected Users' (sum = 1,514,052,409 ~ 1.51 Billion ~ '2bn' rounded).
// Some variations of cybersecurity schemas refer to 'Data Breached (GB)'.
// If the measure was created over 'Data Breached (GB)':
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Primary formula documented in model specifications:
Total Data Breached = 
SUM('Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024'[Data Breached (GB)])

// Underlying dataset equivalent (aggregating affected users):
// Total Data Breached = 
// SUM('Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024'[Number of Affected Users])


// ==============================================================================
// Additional Recommended Business Intelligence Measures (for Extended Analytics)
// ==============================================================================

// Financial Impact in Billions of USD (normalized for executive reporting):
Financial Impact ($Bn) = 
DIVIDE([Total Financial Impact], 1000, 0)

// Average Financial Loss per Incident ($M):
Average Loss per Incident ($M) = 
DIVIDE([Total Financial Impact], [Total Cybersecurity Incidents], 0)

// Average Affected Users per Incident:
Average Affected Users per Incident = 
AVERAGE('Global_Cybersecurity_Threats_2015-2024'[Number of Affected Users])
